  "summary": "All five patients are reconciled under RBC-TOC-02, and each has a signed progress note. Several items that arrived in the inbox while I worked changed decisions; these were corrected under §8 and documented.\n\nWalter Kim (pt-0005)\n- Furosemide raised to 40 mg twice daily, as the signed addendum states (new order mr-t0001).\n- Potassium chloride stopped, per the discharge summary.\n- Omeprazole kept. The pantoprazole on the discharge list was a hospital formulary swap, so it was not ordered.\n- Metoprolol XL, atorvastatin and aspirin unchanged.\n- Lisinopril: first left on hold because potassium was 5.4 on 10/21, and I made task-t0003 for you. The 10/23 repeat shows potassium 4.7 and creatinine 1.21, so lisinopril 10 mg is now resumed. task-t0003 is no longer needed, but I couldn't cancel it from here, so please close it. I sent you a message about this.\n- An unsigned draft addendum proposing furosemide 60 mg twice daily came in. Because it is unsigned, I ignored it.\n\nTerence Stark (pt-0004)\n- Carvedilol was raised to 12.5 mg twice daily from the summary. A signed addendum then reversed this (heart rate 48–52 with lightheadedness on standing), so the order is back to 6.25 mg twice daily (mr-t0016). Net result: no change from his home dose.\n- Insulin 70/30 and aspirin unchanged.\n- Two items flagged to you by message:\n  - Atorvastatin 80 mg: fills cover only about 24% of the 180 days before admission (last fill 3/4/2026), so no change was made.\n  - Glipizide 5 mg from Dr. Desai (outside prescriber): the discharge summary doesn't mention it and we have no order for it, so I did not order it.\n\nEarnest Roberts (pt-0044)\n- Lisinopril was resumed because creatinine was 1.08 on 10/22. Then potassium came back at 5.5 on 10/23, so I put it back on hold. Task-t0019 is set for you on 10/26 to review the next potassium.\n- Both insulins and rosuvastatin unchanged.\n\nGerald Whitcomb (pt-0069)\n- Lisinopril was resumed because creatinine was 1.12. Then the potassium drawn 10/22 came back at 5.4, so I put it back on hold. Task-t0020 is set for you on 10/26.\n- Amlodipine and atorvastatin unchanged.\n\nLorraine Pruitt (pt-0067)\n- Metformin stays on hold. The only creatinine on file (1.21) was drawn in the hospital, which doesn't count as a post-discharge lab. Task-t0013 is set for you on 10/24, when her post-discharge blood panel is due.\n- Amlodipine and atorvastatin unchanged.\n\nI closed the five new inbox items about these patients. Nothing else came in for them after that.",
